{
  "info": {
    "name": "Multi-Network Faucet Service",
    "description": "API collection for testing the Multi-Network Faucet Service\n\n## Supported Networks\n- Sepolia (ETH)\n- Polygon Amoy (POL)\n\n## Two Modes\n1. Normal Mode: Address + network (checks balance, rate limited per network)\n2. Admin Mode: Address + network + master password (bypasses all checks)\n\n## Environments\n- Local: http://localhost:3000\n- Production: https://your-faucet.vercel.app",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json",
    "_postman_id": "12345678-1234-1234-1234-123456789012",
    "_exporter_id": "12345678"
  },
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "🏥 Health & Status",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Health Check",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/health",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "health"]
            },
            "description": "Simple health check endpoint to verify the service is running."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Get Multi-Network Status",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/status",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "status"]
            },
            "description": "Get detailed status for all supported networks including:\n- Faucet address and balance per network\n- Requests remaining per network\n- Network health status\n- Overall service status"
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "🔷 Sepolia Network",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Sepolia - Request ETH (Normal Mode)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"address\": \"0x742d35Cc6634C0532925a3b844Bc9e7595f0bEb\",\n  \"network\": \"sepolia\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/faucet",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "faucet"]
            },
            "description": "Request Sepolia ETH - Normal Mode\n\n**Required:**\n- `address`: Recipient Ethereum address\n- `network`: \"sepolia\"\n\n**Features:**\n- Checks if address has balance (< 0.001 ETH)\n- 24-hour rate limit per address per network\n- Sends 0.005 ETH\n\n**Response:**\n- Transaction hash\n- Amount: \"0.005\"\n- Currency: \"ETH\"\n- Network: \"Sepolia\"\n- Etherscan link"
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"Status code is 200\", function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "pm.test(\"Response has transaction hash\", function () {",
                  "    var jsonData = pm.response.json();",
                  "    pm.expect(jsonData).to.have.property('transactionHash');",
                  "    pm.expect(jsonData.currency).to.eql('ETH');",
                  "    pm.expect(jsonData.network).to.eql('Sepolia');",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "pm.test(\"Transaction hash is valid\", function () {",
                  "    var jsonData = pm.response.json();",
                  "    pm.expect(jsonData.transactionHash).to.match(/^0x[a-fA-F0-9]{64}$/);",
                  "});"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Sepolia - Request ETH (Admin Mode)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"address\": \"0x742d35Cc6634C0532925a3b844Bc9e7595f0bEb\",\n  \"network\": \"sepolia\",\n  \"masterPassword\": \"{{masterPassword}}\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/faucet",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "faucet"]
            },
            "description": "Request Sepolia ETH - Admin Mode\n\n**Required:**\n- `address`: Recipient Ethereum address\n- `network`: \"sepolia\"\n- `masterPassword`: Master password from .env\n\n**Features:**\n- Bypasses balance check\n- Bypasses rate limit\n- Perfect for testing\n\n**Response:**\n- Mode: \"admin\""
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"Status code is 200\", function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "pm.test(\"Admin mode response\", function () {",
                  "    var jsonData = pm.response.json();",
                  "    pm.expect(jsonData.mode).to.eql('admin');",
                  "});"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Sepolia - With Variables",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"address\": \"{{testAddress}}\",\n  \"network\": \"sepolia\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/faucet",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "faucet"]
            },
            "description": "Test Sepolia with environment variable address"
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    },
